This folder contains all the Matlab scripts we use to analyse the radichromic films

FILES EXPLANATION

==> CalibrationRCF.m
This script can be used to calibrate in dose a set of radiochromic. 
It takes RCF images and the corresponding doses values and returns a calibration 
curve with the fitting parameters. The output is stored in a file (CalibrationData.txt) 
that can be read by other scripts (like the ReadRadiochromicDose.m or CalibrationRCF.m itself) 
where the calibration is needed.


==> ReadRadiochromicDose.m
This script can be used to convert in dose the signal of a set of radiochromic films. 
It takes RCF images and, one-by-one, returns the corresponding dose value by using a calibration curve 
with the fitting parameters. The output is stored in a file (CalibrationDataAndFit.txt).


==> UnfoldingNew.m
This script can be used to reconstruct the depth-dose distribution of a stack of radiochromic films and 
the spectrum of the primary protons of the incident beam. It works with all the film images together.
It's currently under review.


==> Test_2025
This folder contains the EBT3 data (both calibration and stack) used as reference for tests.